  "name": "W4 · Gully heads and corridor edge (draft) – corridor edge",
  "notes": "Job: where the western side gullies start and the vine-forest corridor edge begins. Zone 5, left wild.\nWeed control only (molasses grass, lantana and other woody weeds), working in from the edges a little at a time.\nLet local species come back; if gaps need help, plant only local LFW rainforest species.\nNo fruit trees, no earthworks, no burning; leave fallen timber in the gully.\nPlaced at the heads of LiDAR flow lines (2022, 1 m), where water first gathers into a channel.\nDraft from the 19–20 Oct western high edge plan – adjust on site.",
